# Origin of the backend, with no trailing slash and no /api suffix:
#   https://portfolio-manager.up.railway.app
#
# Normally leave this unset - in both development and production.
#
# Locally, Vite's proxy (vite.config.ts) forwards /api and /socket.io to
# port 5000. Deployed, vercel.json rewrites the same two paths to the
# Railway service. Either way the browser only ever talks to its own
# origin, which is what keeps the session cookie first-party: a cookie set
# by a different site is a third-party cookie, and Safari blocks those
# outright while Chrome is phasing them out. Setting this variable points
# the client straight at the backend and reintroduces exactly that
# problem.
#
# It exists as an escape hatch for pointing a local client at some other
# backend. Vite inlines it at build time, so it is visible in the shipped
# bundle - a public URL and nothing secret.
VITE_API_URL=
